<section class="how">
  <h2>How to Use This Love Calculator</h2>
  <p>Type in the first person's name and the second person's name. Click Calculate Love and your score appears with a fun compatibility label. The calculation runs entirely inside your browser so nothing is stored or sent to a server.</p>
  <p>Try entering your own name and a celebrity crush. Try fictional couples from your favourite books or shows. You can also test friends and find out who the algorithm thinks is your best match. The same combination of names will always give the same result, so you can share your score with confidence that your friend will see the exact same number.</p>
</section>

<section class="formula">
  <h2>How the Algorithm Works</h2>
  <p>The calculator converts each character in both names into a numeric value based on its position in the alphabet. It combines both names into a single string, processes the digits through a series of reductions, and produces a final number between 1 and 100.</p>
  <p>This method is a classic love calculator algorithm that has been used on novelty websites since the early days of the internet. It is entirely deterministic and designed for entertainment. The same type of algorithm runs on many popular love test apps and websites.</p>
  <p>Real romantic compatibility research from psychology suggests factors like attachment style, communication patterns, shared goals, and conflict resolution ability are far better predictors of relationship success. This calculator captures none of those things, and that is completely fine because it is meant to be fun.</p>
</section>

