<section class="faq">
  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

  <h3>How does a love calculator work?</h3>
  <p>This tool converts both names into numeric values using a deterministic algorithm and combines them to produce a percentage between 1 and 100. The same two names will always produce the exact same result. It is a novelty entertainment tool rather than a scientific compatibility test.</p>

  <h3>Is the love percentage accurate?</h3>
  <p>No. Real romantic compatibility depends on communication, shared values, emotional availability, and countless personal factors that no name-based algorithm can measure. Think of the score as you would a fortune cookie: fun to read and share, but not something to base life decisions on.</p>

  <h3>Can I use it for celebrity names?</h3>
  <p>Yes, absolutely. Enter any names you like including celebrity couples, fictional characters from books and films, or historical figures. Many people enjoy testing famous pairs to see what result comes up. There are no restrictions on what names you enter.</p>

  <h3>Why do I get the same result every time?</h3>
  <p>The algorithm is intentionally consistent. If it produced a different number each time it would feel random and meaningless. A stable result means you can share your score and your friend will see the same number when they check. It makes the tool feel more like a personality quiz than a coin flip.</p>

  <h3>What is the highest possible love score?</h3>
  <p>The maximum is 100 percent. Scores above 80 get a "perfect match" label. Between 60 and 80 you will see "great connection". Below 60 the tool describes it as "work in progress" and below 30 as "just friends". All of these labels are meant to be taken lightly and with a smile.</p>
</section>

